# Convex Real-time Patterns

## Core Concept

Convex `useQuery` is reactive by default. When the underlying data changes, the query re-runs and the component re-renders with fresh data. There is:

- No `useEffect` for subscriptions
- No manual channel setup or cleanup
- No event listeners
- No missed events (guaranteed consistency)

## Pattern

```typescript
import { useQuery } from "convex/react";
import { api } from "@/convex/_generated/api";

// Single line. Auto-subscribes. Auto-updates. Auto-cleans up.
const gameSession = useQuery(api.gameSessions.getByGame, { gameId });
```

## Active Queries

| Data | Query |
|---|---|
| Game session (phase, speaking order) | `useQuery(api.gameSessions.getByGame, { gameId })` |
| Players (seats, alive, fouls) | `useQuery(api.gamePlayers.listByGame, { gameId })` |
| Game data (host, status) | `useQuery(api.games.getById, { gameId })` |
| Night phase session | `useQuery(api.nightPhaseSessions.getCurrent, { gameId })` |
| Player roles (filtered) | `useQuery(api.gamePlayerRoles.getFiltered, { gameId })` |
| Join request status | `useQuery(api.joinRequests.getMyStatus, { gameId })` |
| Pending join requests | `useQuery(api.joinRequests.listPending, { gameId })` |
| Lobby games | `useQuery(api.games.listAll)` |

## Conditional Queries

Use `"skip"` to conditionally disable a query:

```typescript
const session = useQuery(
  api.gameSessions.getByGame,
  gameId ? { gameId } : "skip"
);
```

## Loading States

`useQuery` returns `undefined` while loading:

```typescript
const gameSession = useQuery(api.gameSessions.getByGame, { gameId });

if (gameSession === undefined) {
  return <LoadingSpinner />;
}

// gameSession is now the actual data (or null if not found)
```

## Combining Multiple Queries

Call multiple `useQuery` hooks in the same component. Each subscribes independently:

```typescript
function GameRoom({ gameId }) {
  const game = useQuery(api.games.getById, { gameId });
  const session = useQuery(api.gameSessions.getByGame, { gameId });
  const players = useQuery(api.gamePlayers.listByGame, { gameId });
  const nightSession = useQuery(
    api.nightPhaseSessions.getCurrent,
    session?.gamePhase === "night_phase" ? { gameId } : "skip"
  );
}
```

## Mutations Trigger Query Updates

```typescript
const castVote = useMutation(api.votes.cast);

// When this mutation completes, any useQuery watching the votes table
// will automatically re-run and update the UI
await castVote({ votingSessionId, voterSeat: 3, seatNumber: 5 });
```

## Performance Notes

- Convex queries only re-run when the specific data they read changes
- No need to debounce (Convex batches updates)
- No need to limit subscriptions (Convex manages connections)
- Convex automatically handles reconnection and catch-up after network issues
